"1. During incoming inspection of a motor control centre (MCC) at a gas processing plant, the QC Inspector verifies the IP rating of the enclosure. The area is classified as Zone 1, gas group IIA, temperature class T3. The MCC enclosure is rated IP54. Is this acceptable for outdoor installation in a Zone 1 classified area?",
"Yes — IP54 provides adequate protection against dust and splash, which is sufficient for outdoor classified areas.\nNo — Zone 1 locations require Ex d (flameproof) or Ex e (increased safety) equipment with the appropriate group and temperature class certification; IP54 alone is not an ignition protection classification and does not qualify the MCC for Zone 1 installation.\nYes — IP54 is the minimum required for outdoor classified areas per SAES-P-111.\nNo — Zone 1 requires IP65 minimum; IP54 is only acceptable for Zone 2.",
